course: dictionary
lesson: 11268
title: Wrestle: fight or struggle
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wrestle is a verb, so it is something you do. It has two meanings. The first is a fight where you hold and push someone, trying to get them down on the ground, as a sport or in play. The second is to struggle hard with a problem or a difficult object.
explain: Look at the words around it to pick the right meaning. «The red kangaroo is the largest marsupial... males wrestle and kick each other with their strong back legs.» Here the males are fighting with their bodies. But «She wrestled with the maths problem» means she worked hard to solve it, so it is about struggling, not fighting.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «she fought hard with the maths problem» make sense? It sounds a bit odd, but «she struggled hard with the maths problem» fits well, so the struggle meaning is right. Always ask: which meaning fits these clues?
fact: Wrestle is a verb. Its other forms are wrestles, wrestled and wrestling.
fact: «Wrestle» means to fight by holding and pushing someone, trying to get them to the ground, as a sport or in play.
fact: «Wrestle» can also mean to struggle hard with a problem, as in «wrestle with homework».
fact: In an old story, «Jacob... wrestled all night and was renamed Israel.»
fact: Wrestling as a sport has rules and referees. Stag beetles use their huge jaws to wrestle, lifting and flipping rivals.
exercise: «The red kangaroo... males wrestle and kick each other with their strong back legs.» What does wrestle mean here? | To be renamed | To hop over fifty kilometres an hour | *To fight by holding and pushing | To sleep quietly in the shade
exercise: Mia says, «I will wrestle with my homework tonight.» What does wrestle mean here? | To read aloud | To run away from the work | *To struggle hard with a problem | To fight by holding and pushing
exercise: Which of these is a sport with rules and referees? | Painting | *Wrestling | Sleeping | Hopping
test: You wrestle with a heavy suitcase. What does this mean? | You hit the suitcase with your fists | You open it and look inside | You put it on a shelf quietly | *You struggle hard to lift and move it
test: «Two brothers in Melbourne broke a vase wrestling.» What does wrestling mean here? | Writing a letter | Singing loudly | *Fighting by holding and pushing each other | Hopping like a kangaroo
exam: In «She wrestled with the maths problem», what does wrestled mean? | To give up at once | *To struggle hard to solve it | To draw a picture of it | To fight a classmate
